 step does (never pass a bare or guessed id to `bd`, which fuzzy-matches and can
 reassign the wrong bead); `$GC_BEAD_ID` is the convoy the molecule was poured
-on. If a clean read shows the work bead is no longer `in_progress` for this
-session, submit-and-exit already ran — drain and exit. Otherwise run it:
+on, and when it is not exported the block below recovers the convoy from the
+step bead you are holding. Only positive evidence — the work bead closed, or
+handed to somebody else — means submit-and-exit already ran. Otherwise run it:
 
 ```bash
 EXPECTED_ASSIGNEE="${BEADS_ACTOR:-${GC_SESSION_NAME:-${GC_SESSION_ID:-${GC_AGENT:-}}}}"
+# `$GC_BEAD_ID` is not always exported — it was empty in gcp-rz8a's session, so
+# this guard could not run at all. Recover the convoy from the molecule root of
+# the step bead this session is holding rather than skipping the check.
+CONVOY_ID="${GC_BEAD_ID:-}"
+if [ -z "$CONVOY_ID" ]; then
+  ROOT_BEAD_ID=$(gc bd list --assignee="$EXPECTED_ASSIGNEE" --status=in_progress \
+    --has-metadata-key gc.step_ref --include-infra --limit=0 --json 2>/dev/null |
+    jq -r '[.[] | .metadata."gc.root_bead_id" // empty] | .[0] // empty' 2>/dev/null)
+  if [ -n "$ROOT_BEAD_ID" ]; then
+    CONVOY_ID=$(gc bd show "$ROOT_BEAD_ID" --json 2>/dev/null |
+      jq -r '.[0].metadata."gc.input_convoy_id" // .[0].metadata."gc.var.convoy_id" // empty' 2>/dev/null)
+  fi
+fi
 # Read the convoy + work bead with retry — same unreadable-is-not-terminal
 # discipline as the claim block above. An unreadable state (empty JSON, a convoy
 # blip, or 0/>=2 children so WORK_BEAD_ID is empty) is NOT proof that
-# submit-and-exit already ran. Only a SUCCESSFUL read showing the bead genuinely
-# moved off this session (closed, or reassigned to refinery) means it is done.
+# submit-and-exit already ran.
 WORK_BEAD_ID=""
 WORK_STATUS=""
 WORK_ASSIGNEE=""
@@ -442,7 +455,7 @@ READ_OK=0
 READ_TRY=0
 while [ "$READ_TRY" -lt 3 ]; do
   READ_TRY=$((READ_TRY + 1))
-  CONVOY_STATUS=$(gc convoy status "$GC_BEAD_ID" --json 2>/dev/null)
+  CONVOY_STATUS=$(gc convoy status "$CONVOY_ID" --json 2>/dev/null)
   WORK_BEAD_ID=$(printf '%s' "$CONVOY_STATUS" | jq -r 'if (.children | length) == 1 then .children[0].id else empty end' 2>/dev/null)
   if [ -n "$WORK_BEAD_ID" ]; then
     WORK_JSON=$(gc bd show "$WORK_BEAD_ID" --json 2>/dev/null)
@@ -456,12 +469,18 @@ while [ "$READ_TRY" -lt 3 ]; do
   fi
   sleep 1
 done
-if [ "$READ_OK" -eq 1 ] && { [ "$WORK_STATUS" != "in_progress" ] || [ "$WORK_ASSIGNEE" != "$EXPECTED_ASSIGNEE" ]; }; then
+# Only POSITIVE evidence counts: the bead is closed, or it is assigned to
+# somebody who is not this session (the refinery). "Not in_progress for me" is
+# NOT evidence — a molecule's work bead is never assigned to the polecat
+# session in the first place, so that test reports already-submitted on work
+# that has not been submitted at all, and drains with the branch unpushed.
+if [ "$READ_OK" -eq 1 ] && { [ "$WORK_STATUS" = "closed" ] ||
+     { [ -n "$WORK_ASSIGNEE" ] && [ "$WORK_ASSIGNEE" != "$EXPECTED_ASSIGNEE" ]; }; }; then
   echo "ALREADY_SUBMITTED $WORK_BEAD_ID status=$WORK_STATUS assignee=$WORK_ASSIGNEE — submit-and-exit already ran; draining."
   gc runtime drain-ack
   exit
 fi
-# Unreadable after retries, or still in_progress for this session: DO NOT assume
+# No positive evidence, or unreadable after retries: DO NOT assume
 # already-submitted — fall through and run submit-and-exit. A stranded
 # in_progress bead with an unpushed branch is the worse outcome.
 ```
diff --git a/gastown/formulas/mol-polecat-work.toml b/gastown/formulas/mol-polecat-work.toml
index 778d2d09..ad5ec249 100644
--- a/gastown/formulas/mol-polecat-work.toml
+++ b/gastown/formulas/mol-polecat-work.toml
@@ -17,9 +17,12 @@ merge review.
 The polecat sets `metadata.branch` and `metadata.target` on the work bead
 and reassigns it to the refinery. The refinery merges and closes.
 
-**NEVER CLOSE BEADS.** You must not run `gc bd close` or set status=closed.
-Even if you believe the code is already merged, reassign to refinery —
-only the refinery verifies merges and closes beads.
+**NEVER CLOSE THE WORK BEAD.** You must not run `gc bd close` or set
+status=closed on it. Even if you believe the code is already merged, reassign
+to refinery — only the refinery verifies merges and closes beads. The single
+exception is your own formula step beads: `submit-and-exit` closes its own
+step (resolved with `gc hook current`) before draining, because a step left
+claimed is handed back to the pool and re-run.
 `{{base_branch}}` may come from the work bead's own `metadata.target` or
 be inherited from a parent convoy with `metadata.target` set.
 
@@ -658,6 +661,47 @@ needs = ["self-review"]
 description = """
 Hand off your work and self-clean. You cease to exist after this step.
 
+**0. Already-submitted guard (idempotent re-entry).**
+
+A re-entered submit-and-exit must not re-write bead state. Step 6 sets the
+assignee and clears `gc.routed_to`; run a second time on a bead the refinery
+has since parked, it silently pulls that bead back out of an escalation
+(gcp-rz8a). Bail out before touching anything when all three marks of a
+completed handoff are present — target recorded, branch on origin at this
+commit, and the bead handed to somebody who is not this session:
+
+```bash
+CONVOY_STATUS=$(gc convoy status {{convoy_id}} --json)
+WORK_BEAD_ID=$(printf '%s' "$CONVOY_STATUS" | jq -r 'if (.children | length) == 1 then .children[0].id else empty end')
+STEP_SESSION="${BEADS_ACTOR:-${GC_SESSION_NAME:-${GC_SESSION_ID:-${GC_AGENT:-}}}}"
+SUBMITTED_JSON=$(gc bd show "$WORK_BEAD_ID" --json)
+SUBMITTED_TARGET=$(printf '%s' "$SUBMITTED_JSON" | jq -r '.[0].metadata.target // empty')
+SUBMITTED_BRANCH=$(printf '%s' "$SUBMITTED_JSON" | jq -r '.[0].metadata.branch // empty')
+SUBMITTED_ASSIGNEE=$(printf '%s' "$SUBMITTED_JSON" | jq -r '.[0].assignee // empty')
+SUBMITTED_REMOTE=""
+if [ -n "$SUBMITTED_BRANCH" ]; then
+    SUBMITTED_REMOTE=$(git ls-remote origin "refs/heads/$SUBMITTED_BRANCH" 2>/dev/null | awk '{print $1}')
+fi
+if [ -n "$SUBMITTED_TARGET" ] && [ -n "$SUBMITTED_REMOTE" ] &&
+   [ "$SUBMITTED_REMOTE" = "$(git rev-parse HEAD)" ] &&
+   [ -n "$SUBMITTED_ASSIGNEE" ] && [ "$SUBMITTED_ASSIGNEE" != "$STEP_SESSION" ]; then
+    echo "ALREADY_SUBMITTED $WORK_BEAD_ID target=$SUBMITTED_TARGET branch=$SUBMITTED_BRANCH assignee=$SUBMITTED_ASSIGNEE"
+    echo "Handoff already completed. Closing this step and draining without re-writing bead state."
+    STEP_BEAD_ID=$(gc hook current --id-only) || exit 1  # drain-ack gives back every claim this session still holds, so close this step first
+    STEP_BEAD=$(gc bd show "$STEP_BEAD_ID" --json) || exit 1
+    printf '%s' "$STEP_BEAD" | jq -e '(if type == "array" then .[0] else . end) | .status == "in_progress" and ((.metadata["gc.step_ref"] // "") | endswith(".submit-and-exit"))' >/dev/null || { echo "submit-and-exit: current claim $STEP_BEAD_ID is not this in-progress step; not acknowledging drain" >&2; exit 1; }
+    gc bd update "$STEP_BEAD_ID" --set-metadata gc.outcome=pass --status=closed || exit 1
+    gc runtime drain-ack
+    exit 0
+fi
+```
+
+All three marks are required together on purpose. `metadata.target` alone
+proves nothing — a caller may set it before dispatch to choose the base branch
+— and an unassigned bead with the branch on origin is the shape a witness
+salvage push leaves behind (gcp-7bo9), which is not a handoff this step
+performed.
+
 **1. Branch-shape gate (fails closed — non-negotiable).**
 
 Before anything else, verify you are on a per-bead branch. The refinery
@@ -1221,6 +1265,28 @@ carries the marker.
 **6. Reassign to refinery:**
 ```bash
 REFINERY_TARGET="${GC_RIG:+$GC_RIG/}{{binding_prefix}}refinery"
+# NEVER clear gc.routed_to when it reads `human`. That value is an operator
+# escalation — the refinery writes it when it REFUSES to land a bead, typically
+# on an armed require_merge_approval gate. Reassigning to the refinery there
+# does not resume the work, it silently undoes the one control that makes
+# reviewed merges real (gcp-rz8a). The branch is already pushed and recorded, so
+# halting here loses nothing: the human owns the next move.
+ROUTED_TO=$(gc bd show "$WORK_BEAD_ID" --json 2>/dev/null | jq -r '.[0].metadata."gc.routed_to" // empty')
+if [ "$ROUTED_TO" = "human" ]; then
+    echo "HANDOFF HALTED: $WORK_BEAD_ID is routed to human — an operator escalation."
+    echo "Branch is pushed and metadata.target is set; leaving assignee and gc.routed_to untouched."
+    gc bd note "$WORK_BEAD_ID" --stdin <<'HUMAN_HALT'
+Polecat submit-and-exit halted at the refinery handoff: gc.routed_to=human.
+Branch is pushed and metadata.target is recorded. Assignee and routing left as
+the escalation set them; a human decides whether this goes to the refinery.
+HUMAN_HALT
+    STEP_BEAD_ID=$(gc hook current --id-only) || exit 1  # drain-ack gives back every claim this session still holds, so close this step first
+    STEP_BEAD=$(gc bd show "$STEP_BEAD_ID" --json) || exit 1
+    printf '%s' "$STEP_BEAD" | jq -e '(if type == "array" then .[0] else . end) | .status == "in_progress" and ((.metadata["gc.step_ref"] // "") | endswith(".submit-and-exit"))' >/dev/null || { echo "submit-and-exit: current claim $STEP_BEAD_ID is not this in-progress step; not acknowledging drain" >&2; exit 1; }
+    gc bd update "$STEP_BEAD_ID" --set-metadata gc.outcome=fail --set-metadata gc.failure_class=hard --set-metadata gc.failure_reason=routed_to_human --status=closed || exit 1
+    gc runtime drain-ack
+    exit 0
+fi
 gc bd update "$WORK_BEAD_ID" --status=open --assignee="$REFINERY_TARGET" --set-metadata gc.routed_to=""
 # The handoff is the assignee write; `--status=open` is bookkeeping that has
 # been observed not to stick (gcp-s14g). Read it back and correct it once, so
